# Security headers for the static site, served by Cloudflare Workers assets
# (same syntax as Cloudflare Pages / Netlify `_headers`). Applied to every
# response under the matched path.
#
# CSP notes:
#  - script-src is 'self' only (plus the GA host) — deliberately NO
#    'unsafe-inline', so an injected <script> or onerror= handler is blocked.
#    The site has no inline <script> that must run today. When GA is enabled
#    (the commented gtag block in index.html/writing.html), either move its
#    inline init into a .js file OR add its sha256 hash here — do NOT add
#    'unsafe-inline', which would defeat the XSS protection below.
#  - style-src allows 'unsafe-inline' because the feed renderer emits inline
#    style="" attributes (badges). Style injection is low-risk; script is not.
#  - connect-src allows the Decile form relay and self (insights.json fetch).
#  - img-src allows https: so Notion-hosted covers render even if a sync ever
#    skips the local download step.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://www.googletagmanager.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https:; connect-src 'self' https://shuckervc-decile-relay.shuckervcwebsite.workers.dev https://www.google-analytics.com https://region1.google-analytics.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
